      "writtenOn": "2019-07-26T17:53:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Before returning, you should check that there are no samples. We\u0027ve run into this with the lsm6dsm before:\n1. Check status register, get N readings\n2. Read N readings\n3. While you were reading you got a new sample, this means that the interrupt never triggered and you missed updating last_interrupt_timestamp\n\nThe fix is to re-check the count. If you still have values, update the last_interrupt_timestamp and set the task event (basically a fake call to lis2dw12_interrupt). See http://cs/chromeos_public/src/platform/ec/driver/accelgyro_lsm6dsm.c?l\u003d496 for reference.",
      "revId": "e4d1eab12d649b122df5ae7f1e37f8eea91f2a3b",
